WEBVTT

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.420
Wassup?!

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.710
<b>HERE</b>

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:07.750
Allow me to introduce you.
This is my cute little navigator, Mikael.

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:10.250
A fusion of mikan and frog! The orange color is so cute!

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:11.380
Don't touch him!

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.000
Huh?

00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:15.630
Mikael is a golden poison frog,
so touching him is deadly.

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:16.920
Just a touch is deadly?!

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:20.420
Whenever we get into a serious fight,
he transforms into a magical arrow for me!

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.500
He's very reliable!

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.380
An arrow that can insta-kill...

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.670
You really like to read, huh, Ryo?

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:27.210
Yeah!

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:36.330
<b>A HISTORY OF</b>

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:36.330
<b>PURGES AND BETRAYALS</b>

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:36.330
<b>IN ANCIENT CHINA</b>

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.630
All the books I've been reading lately are ones
to help with your quest for world domination.

00:00:32.210 --> 00:00:34.880
A history of purges and betrayals in ancient China.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.330
That's a pretty sinister title!

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.250
Assassinations are so terrifying...

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.290
You're still in elementary school, Ryo!
Try reading something more lighthearted!

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.290
<b>FAIRY TALE SERIES</b>

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:42.290
<b>THE MONKEY-CRAB BATTLE</b>

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.960
<b>FAIRY TALE SERIES</b>

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:44.960
<b>THE MONKEY-CRAB BATTLE</b>

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:44.920
So they use a surprise attack
to lure the target into favorable terrain...

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.460
With all the profound strategy and coordination
based around personal skills in here,

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:49.880
I can't believe this is a fairy tale!

00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:51.290
Her learning proficiency is too good!

00:00:52.880 --> 00:00:56.330
Jeez, Shamiko. Why do you always
go to school in that silly uniform?

00:00:56.330 --> 00:00:57.830
Because it's part of the dress code.

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:00.540
Forget rules like that, they only deny
individualism and enforce conformity!

00:01:00.790 --> 00:01:03.540
Demons like us are associated with chaos by nature!

00:01:03.540 --> 00:01:05.920
We must rebel against all forms of order!
So go to school naked!

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.040
<b>NAKED</b>

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.000
But I'll get arrested!

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:10.130
My uniform is great because
I never have to stress about what to wear.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:12.290
Plus, it uses good quality fabric that feels comfy!

00:01:12.290 --> 00:01:15.250
I refuse to accept this! Grow a darn spine, you wussy!

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:21.170
Oh, now I see. This is nice.
I could definitely wear this every day.

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.710
You look adorable, Ancestor!

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:58.040
<b>URBAN EXPLORATION!</b>

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:58.040
<b>THE TROUBLED MIKAN AND THE EXCITED DEMON</b>

00:02:58.040 --> 00:02:59.630
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:02:58.830 --> 00:03:01.170
Huh? What are you doing out here, Mikan?

00:03:01.290 --> 00:03:03.710
I'm searching for an apartment complex that's nearby.

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.580
All of a sudden, I found myself living with
magical girls on either side of me.

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:07.670
<b>GLOOOOOOM...</b>

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.460
And for whatever reason, Momo gifted us red meat
which we used to have a welcome party.

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.080
<b>DOOM</b>

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.080
<b>DOOM</b>

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:10.080
<b>DOOM</b>

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:11.000
<b>KAWHAAAAM!</b>

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.830
<b>RED</b>

00:03:11.130 --> 00:03:12.830
<b>RED</b>

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:12.830
<b>RED</b>

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:12.830
<b>RED</b>

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:14.670
I'm going to use everything
I have to make this a success!

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:15.920
Calm down, Momo!

00:03:15.920 --> 00:03:17.580
The food is starting to glow!

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.250
Things got a little crazy
when Momo transformed while I wasn't looking.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.330
And lemon juice was flying all over the place.

00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:29.040
Before long, the party was in full tilt.

00:03:29.170 --> 00:03:31.630
By the way, what exactly is a "tilt" anyway?

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:34.630
Well, let's not sweat the small stuff right now.

00:03:34.630 --> 00:03:37.290
Because we gotta focus on solving
the mysteries of the past!

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:40.290
Oh, yeah!

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:44.040
I should make an offering of this tasty meat
to dad's spirit in the box.

00:03:44.420 --> 00:03:45.290
How strange.

00:03:45.290 --> 00:03:47.000
What's the matter, Mikan?

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:47.880
That box...

00:03:47.580 --> 00:03:51.080
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:51.040
It looks exactly like the ones
my family uses at our factory.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:51.710
Huh?

00:03:51.710 --> 00:03:55.880
I actually have a bunch in my room right now.
I used them to move my stuff.

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:56.880
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:56.880
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:57.420
See?

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.380
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.380
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:03:56.880 --> 00:03:59.380
<b>TADAAAAH</b>

00:03:57.630 --> 00:03:59.330
My dad is all over the place!

00:03:59.960 --> 00:04:01.540
I'm really confused.

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:08.080
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:04:01.710 --> 00:04:08.080
So, like, does this mean that my sister sealed
Mr. Joshua inside of an ordinary packing box?

00:04:08.710 --> 00:04:09.670
Come now, girls.

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.290
Let's just enjoy the welcome party.
You can think about that later.

00:04:13.290 --> 00:04:14.960
You're way too calm about all this, ma'am!

00:04:15.670 --> 00:04:16.750
Here's an idea.

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:20.000
Let's make things interesting by mixing dad in there
and guessing which one he is!

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:21.330
I bet I can tell him apart.

00:04:22.130 --> 00:04:23.750
That's nice, but let's not.

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:24.960
Aw, but why?

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.460
Don't give up, Shamiko! You'll hurt my feelings
if you pick the wrong box and fail the quiz.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:27.040
It's okay, I can pick the right one...

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.460
Please just put the box, I mean, your husband down.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:33.330
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.330
Keep it down, boy. It's still early.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:40.210
<b>MIKAN</b>

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:37.710
The ruins of the factory where I used to live
are on the outskirts of this town.

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.170
And these boxes were once used there.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:44.830
Really? Then we might find a hint about what happened
to my dad somewhere in those ruins.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.080
It's definitely possible.

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:47.380
Let's check it out.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:51.130
Oh, Yuko... and our young magical girl guests...

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.210
You're setting out on a journey
to search for Dad, aren't you?

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.580
Mom?! You're not looking too good!

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:58.960
Urp, ugh... p-please stop. Just hold me straight.

00:04:59.830 --> 00:05:01.710
I'm so hungover that it's embarrassing...

00:05:01.710 --> 00:05:04.830
I'm seeing a wonderful hallucination
where dad has multiplied!

00:05:04.830 --> 00:05:07.170
Listen, Mom! What you're seeing is totally real!

00:05:07.210 --> 00:05:09.830
<b>YOSHIDA</b>

00:05:09.830 --> 00:05:12.540
Mikan's old house was decimated
because of something my sister did,

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.290
so she bought the land from Mikan's parents.

00:05:14.290 --> 00:05:15.460
Is that what happened?

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.250
If nothing's changed, then it should still be
Ms. Sakura's private property.

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:23.330
I'm going home to fetch the key.
You two go ahead without me.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.750
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.540
You've been there once before, Shamiko.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.710
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.710
<b>KEEP OUT</b>

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:28.710
<b>AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY</b>

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.500
Th-this place is...

00:05:29.540 --> 00:05:31.630
Tick-tock, tick-tock, tick-tock.

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:34.290
...a factory of CATastrophic nightMAREs!

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.420
<b>CAT MARE</b>

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:34.420
<b>CAT MARE</b>

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:38.460
<b>CAT MARE</b>

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.330
We never made anything like that!

00:05:36.330 --> 00:05:38.290
We only made wonderful treats!

00:05:40.250 --> 00:05:43.500
So what happened that made the factory get destroyed?

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.040
Well, there was a time when our factory
saw a sharp decline in business.

00:05:47.250 --> 00:05:51.330
It put my daddy in a really tough spot, which drove him
to perform a ritual that is explicitly forbidden.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:53.040
Your dad performed a ritual?!

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.670
What do you mean by ritual? What kinda ritual was it?!

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:58.290
Uh, well, it was a devil summoning ritual...

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.790
Devil summoning?! What else can you
tell me about your dad?

00:06:00.790 --> 00:06:04.330
If you must know, my daddy is a bearded gentleman
who looks great in a food-processing frock.

00:06:04.540 --> 00:06:05.960
Tell me more!

00:06:05.960 --> 00:06:07.630
Why are you so worked up about this?!

00:06:07.790 --> 00:06:11.330
I'm sorry, but you just keep mentioning
all this exciting stuff!

00:06:12.250 --> 00:06:15.500
My daddy made a wish to keep
his factory and his family safe.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.670
He managed to summon a pretty famous devil

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:22.080
by using a bootleg catalyst
and an incantation he copied from someone else.

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.920
But that little imp twisted
the meaning of my daddy's wish,

00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:27.000
and ultimately put a curse on me, his only daughter,

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.380
which literally destroys anything that causes me trouble.

00:06:29.420 --> 00:06:32.170
How terrible! That's an F in language
comprehension for sure!

00:06:32.380 --> 00:06:36.750
My daddy made a mistake in trying to get
such an enormous wish granted so easily.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:39.330
Because the devil exploited that against him.

00:06:40.250 --> 00:06:44.750
<b>HINATSUKI</b>

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:44.540
He should've known that any wishes
we take shortcuts to fulfill aren't real wishes.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.080
People's desires to take shortcuts can be exploited...

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:49.040
I see. I never considered that.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:51.330
What are you taking notes for?
Wow, that's deep! Really deep!<b></b>

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:55.330
And on top of that, the devil just decided
to start living in my heart,

00:06:55.330 --> 00:06:58.170
and absorbed all the energy of the things
I destroyed to grow even stronger.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:01.960
That's why I went to Ms. Sakura for help.

00:07:01.960 --> 00:07:04.580
And that was when Momo and I met for the very first time.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:05.580
Momo!

00:07:05.580 --> 00:07:08.630
Can you tell me what Momo was like
when she was young?

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:12.040
Well, if I had to describe her,
I would say she was like an angel from Heaven!

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.330
Momo was an angel?!

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:13.330
<b>KAZAAAAP</b>

00:07:13.460 --> 00:07:13.960
<b>WHOA!</b>

00:07:14.210 --> 00:07:15.380
You wanna hear more?

00:07:15.380 --> 00:07:16.460
I sure do!

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:18.460
Hurry up before the monster Momo
comes and gets on our case!

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.460
Sure thing! I'll tell you all about her!

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.460
<b>Tee Hee Hee</b>

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.460
<b>Tee Hee Hee</b>

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.460
<b>Giggle Giggle</b>

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:22.460
<b>Giggle Giggle</b>

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:25.170
<b>10 YEARS AGO</b>

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:46.580
Nice to meet you. My name's Momo.

00:07:47.290 --> 00:07:48.250
Momo?

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:50.920
The magical girl named Sakura Chiyoda
asked me to come here.

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.460
I'm going to look after you
until the situation gets under control.

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:56.460
There should have been a huge lock
on the warehouse door...

00:07:57.170 --> 00:07:58.210
I didn't have trouble opening it.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.080
It's busted!

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:03.000
You can't just barge in on my hiding place like this!

00:08:04.710 --> 00:08:07.630
Come on, Mikan. I know you haven't had
a bite to eat in days.

00:08:08.290 --> 00:08:10.580
Also, it's really cold in here.

00:08:12.170 --> 00:08:16.210
Anybody who gets too close to me
is sent to the hospital sooner or later.

00:08:16.540 --> 00:08:18.920
I even ended up hurting my mommy...

00:08:18.920 --> 00:08:21.460
That's why I decided never to leave this place again!

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.330
Stay away from me or my curse will activate!

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:51.630
It's all right.

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:55.040
I'm super strong, so your curse won't hurt me.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:57.040
So...

00:08:57.500 --> 00:09:00.580
You can cry all you want. Just don't do it alone.

00:09:05.540 --> 00:09:07.580
Thank you, Momo!

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.670
You're hungry, aren't you? I brought you some food.

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.500
What is this?

00:09:15.500 --> 00:09:17.750
I tried to make... riceballs.

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.330
Why are they pink?

00:09:19.880 --> 00:09:21.460
I have no idea...

00:09:22.250 --> 00:09:26.500
The devil inside of me was subdued
and tranquilized thanks to Ms. Sakura's help.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:29.920
But the factory ended up in shambles afterwards
and I had to move away from here.

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:34.330
Still, I'll never forget the words
Momo shared with me back then.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:36.000
So that's how the two of you met.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:37.880
That's such a wonderful memory!

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:44.170
<b>TREMBLE</b>

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:44.170
<b>TREMBLE</b>

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:46.960
<b>TREMBLE</b>

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:46.960
<b>TREMBLE</b>

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:46.960
<b>TREMBLE</b>

00:09:38.750 --> 00:09:46.960
<b>TREMBLE</b>

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:46.960
<b>TREMBLE</b>

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:41.500
The only thing I don't remember
is what those pink things tasted like.

00:09:41.500 --> 00:09:43.460
But I think I enjoyed them. Probably.

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:46.790
Do you have any other stories of Momo being an angel?

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:48.580
Let's see...

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:50.000
<b>Fufufu</b>

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:51.210
Back when Momo was younger,
whenever she transformed she would do this cute danc-

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.330
Story time is over.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:54.960
Crap, monster Momo is here!

00:09:57.000 --> 00:10:00.170
I have many special memories of that warehouse.

00:10:00.630 --> 00:10:01.330
The gate's open.

00:10:02.420 --> 00:10:06.000
It's filled with both my painful
and happy experiences of the past.

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:07.750
It makes me nostalgic.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:11.580
Huh?

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:12.960
It's destroyed!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:16.170
No! The warehouse that contained my salty-sweet,
mikan-flavored memories is gone!

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:17.960
It's been totally wiped off the map!

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.130
Just stay cool, Mikan.

00:10:21.130 --> 00:10:24.670
I'm freaking the heck out! You said I could
unleash my curse on you all I want, right?!

00:10:24.670 --> 00:10:26.630
Prepare to suffer because
I'm laying it on you for life, dang it!

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:29.040
That's not exactly what I said...

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.790
How did the warehouse I was so fond of
get blown to bits?!

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:36.460
I heard the whole factory was decimated
when my sister suppressed the devil inside of you.

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:39.750
But it was only the factory's machinery and infrastructure
that were damaged because of that!

00:10:39.750 --> 00:10:41.920
The warehouse was still very much intact!

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:44.080
I know because I looked at it
one last time before moving away!

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:45.710
<b>GOODBYE,</b>

00:10:41.960 --> 00:10:45.710
<b>OLD FRIEND.</b>

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:45.790
And I remember that clearly!

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.960
Are you sure you didn't confuse it with someplace else?

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.580
Maybe this is another thing you forgot
because of the pink food.

00:10:51.580 --> 00:10:53.790
No, I just wiped that part from my memory on purpose.

00:10:54.170 --> 00:10:56.750
So, hey, could you two stop talking about my cooking?

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:00.170
Everything is decked out in pink!
Come on down to the Pink Food Festival coming soo-

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:00.170
<b>PINK FOOD FEST!!</b>

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:01.420
Not happening.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:09.630
I came to this factory shortly after my sister disappeared
and the warehouse was destroyed at that point.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.250
Shamiko, notebook please.

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.250
Oh, sure!

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:15.290
Wait! I just did what you asked without thinking!

00:11:13.420 --> 00:11:15.290
I need to sort out the timeline here...

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:17.420
Jeez, this pen hardly works.
Don't you dare start treating me like your secretary!<b></b>

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:19.210
Darn you! Darn you!

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>GOALS FOR SUMMER VACATION</b>

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>PLUNGE THE PINK GIRL INTO DARKNESS!!</b>

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>Benefit from taking</b>

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>the easy way -*</b>

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>Somehow make it work so</b>

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>that Momo falls to the dark side!!</b>

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>1) Take advantage of weakness</b>

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>Suggest taking a shortcut</b>

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>Eggplant          Frying pan</b>

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>Cucumber       Ask Momo if</b>

00:11:19.220 --> 00:11:21.330
<b>Plastic wrap    it's okay to buy</b>

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:21.040
What is this?

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.330
"Take advantage of weakness"?

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.580
Oh crap! Don't read that! Don't turn the page!

00:11:25.460 --> 00:11:29.330
The mark that's left here was definitely from
Ms. Sakura's special attack, the Sakurament Cannon!

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:31.250
Oh boy, even more exciting stuff!

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:34.000
So what does the Sakurament Cannon attack do?!

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:36.130
Sorry, I'm busy thinking right now. Save it for later.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:38.040
You'll really tell me about it later?!

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:39.250
Uh, yeah, totally.

00:11:39.250 --> 00:11:40.500
That didn't sound convincing.

00:11:40.670 --> 00:11:44.750
Sakurament Cannon creates a bunch
of cherry blossom-shaped prisms that fly around

00:11:44.750 --> 00:11:48.630
and then turn everything pink
before unleashing a huge laser that goes "Kablamo"!

00:11:48.880 --> 00:11:49.880
Oh wow!

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:52.040
By the way, Fresh Peach
Heart Shower creates a... mpgh!

00:11:52.040 --> 00:11:53.330
You two need to shut your little traps!

00:11:53.330 --> 00:11:55.130
MIKAAAAAN!

00:11:56.250 --> 00:11:59.000
I get the impression my sister destroyed this place twice.

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.420
<b>10 YEARS AGO</b>

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.420
<b>Mikan is cursed</b>

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.420
<b>-* Situation resolved</b>

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.420
<b>* Factory destroyed (1st time)</b>

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.420
<b>Warehouse is still intact</b>

00:11:59.210 --> 00:12:02.420
<b>(Mikan was eyewitness)</b>

00:11:59.580 --> 00:12:01.630
The first time was when she saved Mikan.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:05.960
Then the second time was probably when she fought
alongside Mr. Joshua just before going missing.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.960
<b>9 YEARS AGO</b>

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.960
<b>Sakura goes missing</b>

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.960
<b>(Mr. Joshua is sealed away)</b>

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.960
<b>* Factory destroyed</b>

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.960
<b>Momo returns to town</b>

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.960
<b>Inspects the factory</b>

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:05.960
<b>Warehouse destroyed</b>

00:12:06.170 --> 00:12:09.960
So, basically, these are the traces
that Ms. Sakura left behind before disappearing.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:11.630
Let's check out the warehouse wreckage.

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.790
Shamiko, do you have a shovel or something like that?

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:16.250
It's pretty obvious that I don't!

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:18.080
Then there's only one thing to do.
We'll have to use our hands.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:23.880
Don't give up, Shamiko! Become a demon
who can easily adapt to all sorts of situations!

00:12:39.540 --> 00:12:42.710
Remind me, what exactly are we searching for again?

00:12:42.960 --> 00:12:46.790
Clues to my sister's whereabouts.
The best thing would be if we could find her core.

00:12:46.790 --> 00:12:47.420
"Core"?

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:50.170
All magical girls have their own core.

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:52.750
Even if their magic power gets dispersed,
the core should remain behind.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:55.250
And what are these cores shaped like?

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:58.250
We don't know. It depends on the heart
of whoever it belongs to.

00:12:58.500 --> 00:13:01.000
So we're searching without knowing what it looks like?

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:05.670
That could be a problem if it looks like a discarded glove,
or dead cicada, or some other common thing.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:08.630
Relax, they don't take incoherent shapes like that.

00:13:06.920 --> 00:13:08.630
This is gonna be tough...

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:11.080
It should look like something magical. Hopefully.

00:13:11.710 --> 00:13:13.710
I'm going to search over on this side.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:17.380
Hey, Shamiko?

00:13:17.380 --> 00:13:17.920
Yes?

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:21.670
You know, I think that Momo
used to smile a lot more in the past.

00:13:21.670 --> 00:13:23.830
Now she seems like more of a stiff.

00:13:23.830 --> 00:13:26.710
Do you think it's because she can't find her sister?

00:13:26.710 --> 00:13:28.290
I'm sure that's part of it, but...

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:31.040
I teamed up with her a number of times
during elementary school

00:13:31.040 --> 00:13:32.750
and I remember her being more cheerful.

00:13:32.750 --> 00:13:33.330
Really?

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:36.670
But now she gets all snappy
whenever I try to bring up the past,

00:13:36.670 --> 00:13:39.540
and she's beefed up her muscles
way more than necessary.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:41.040
Do you think something happened?

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:45.880
Momo once told me that she augments
her physical strength with magic.

00:13:45.880 --> 00:13:47.750
Is digging up huge boulders like that normal?!

00:13:47.880 --> 00:13:48.290
Fling.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:51.000
I'll be honest, that's a little freaky even for magical girls.

00:13:51.830 --> 00:13:54.080
Momo hardly ever smiles from what I've seen.

00:13:54.630 --> 00:13:57.790
There was one time she brought me
to this factory to train my magic powers.

00:13:57.790 --> 00:14:00.380
And that was one of the few times
she seemed to be in good spirits.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:04.830
But it's probably because she was amused
by this embarrassing thing that I said.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.130
What did you say?

00:14:06.420 --> 00:14:08.630
It was, "I hope that everyone will..."

00:14:08.630 --> 00:14:09.710
Look over there.

00:14:09.710 --> 00:14:10.630
What?

00:14:12.210 --> 00:14:14.830
Did you say something just now, Mikan?

00:14:14.830 --> 00:14:16.630
Huh? I didn't say anything.

00:14:17.380 --> 00:14:19.290
I heard someone's voice...

00:14:19.830 --> 00:14:21.580
Hold on, where are you going?

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:26.460
Oh my gosh!

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:28.790
I... I found a thing!

00:14:29.080 --> 00:14:30.380
<b>YOU GOT A WEAPON!!</b>

00:14:31.080 --> 00:14:33.630
Momomomomomomomomomomo!

00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:33.630
What's up?

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:36.330
A clue! I just found a potential clue!

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:37.580
Look!

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:39.790
It's some kinda wand!

00:14:41.210 --> 00:14:42.790
Pretty sure that's just a fork.

00:14:43.170 --> 00:14:44.210
Huh? What the?!

00:14:44.540 --> 00:14:47.080
No! It was definitely a wand before! But how?

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:48.920
Shamiko, are you hungry or something?

00:14:48.920 --> 00:14:50.170
Don't give me that look!

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:52.460
How do you confuse a fork with a wand?

00:14:52.460 --> 00:14:53.630
I didn't!

00:14:53.630 --> 00:14:56.420
I heard a voice coming from somewhere
that was telling me to dig in a certain spot!

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:56.830
Voice?

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:01.580
<b>HUFF</b>

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:01.580
<b>HUFF</b>

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:01.580
<b>HUFF</b>

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:01.580
<b>HUFF</b>

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:01.580
<b>HUFF</b>

00:14:56.960 --> 00:15:01.540
It was a wand when I dug it up! But then it
suddenly turned into a fork without me knowing!

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:02.580
She's seeing things.

00:15:02.580 --> 00:15:04.000
And having auditory hallucinations, too.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:04.960
Uh oh...

00:15:04.960 --> 00:15:08.040
Come on! I told you to stop giving me those looks!
I'm telling the honest truth here!

00:15:08.210 --> 00:15:10.420
I'm sorry. We've been out in the heat too long, huh?

00:15:10.420 --> 00:15:13.250
And those horns of yours
make it hard to wear a hat to stay cool...

00:15:13.250 --> 00:15:15.000
Quit pitying me!

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:24.630
<b>TODAY'S</b>

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:24.630
<b>ANRI & OGURA ADVENTURE</b>

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.670
Welcome to the part of the show
where we catch up with Anri and Ogura!

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:22.880
Huh? Since when did we start doing this?

00:15:22.880 --> 00:15:24.630
I'm pretty sure this is the first and last time.

00:15:24.630 --> 00:15:25.830
Great work today!

00:15:25.830 --> 00:15:27.540
Thanks, I'm exhausted.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:30.080
Ugh, it's way too hot out.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:32.830
Gotta be global warming. Earth is so screwed.

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:35.130
That being said, I'm still gonna give it my all tomorrow!

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:35.830
Huh?

00:15:37.420 --> 00:15:39.460
Whoa, that's super sus...

00:15:41.710 --> 00:15:42.920
Whewie!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:45.210
Hi Sata! It's hot out today, huh?

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:46.920
Whatcha wearing that costume for?

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.330
Because I like it!

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:50.040
Isn't it kinda stuffy?

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:51.250
It's tolerable!

00:15:51.380 --> 00:15:53.750
Aren't you curious to know what I'm up to?

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:55.330
Nope! Not even in the slightest!

00:15:55.330 --> 00:15:58.460
Check this out! It's the most
handy thing ever, homunculus clay!

00:15:58.460 --> 00:16:00.540
Cool! Don't worry, I can see it fine from here!

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.210
See how it's moving a bit?

00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:06.080
I'm making sure it grows nice and big
by giving it a sun bath! And lots of love!

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.170
Ba-dump! Ba-dump!

00:16:07.170 --> 00:16:09.790
Look! It's so excited to meet you, Sata!

00:16:09.790 --> 00:16:12.500
Wanna touch it? Go ahead and touch it!

00:16:12.880 --> 00:16:15.210
No, I'm good! Thanks for the offer though!

00:16:15.210 --> 00:16:19.080
I just know that some day
it'll prove really useful to Shamiko.

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:21.420
Oh. I gotta go and help run the shop!

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:22.500
Catch ya later!

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.000
Bye! Good luck!

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:29.330
<b>MARUMA'S MEATS</b>

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:28.170
Maruma's Meats is pleased to deliver meat
and happiness to a dining table near you!

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.330
Come check us out!

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:37.790
<b>TODAY'S</b>

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:37.790
<b>ANRI & OGURA ADVENTURE</b>

00:16:29.340 --> 00:16:37.790
<b>THAT'S ALL FOR NOW</b>

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:33.330
Remember that beef sukiyaki? It was so yummy! I love it!

00:16:33.330 --> 00:16:34.830
And beef grilled with salt!

00:16:34.830 --> 00:16:35.880
That was yummy, too!

00:16:36.250 --> 00:16:37.750
What is this? What's happening?

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:40.830
Enough of this nonsense.
It's time to get back to the story!

00:16:40.830 --> 00:16:42.040
Okay.

00:16:42.290 --> 00:16:47.250
<b>BANDA TERRACE</b>

00:16:43.330 --> 00:16:46.210
Quiet, boy. Don't make such a fuss after dark.

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.460
<b>YOSHIDA</b>

00:16:48.000 --> 00:16:49.420
Welcome, Ms. Momo!

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:50.460
Thanks for having me.

00:16:50.460 --> 00:16:52.540
It was a wand, I swear!

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.630
A rod that transformed the instant you grabbed it...

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:57.920
Mom is drawing something.

00:16:57.920 --> 00:17:01.330
Yuko. Do you remember if it looked anything like this?

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.290
Yes! That's it! It was a cute looking wand just like that!

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:08.960
This is a huge deal, Yuko! I'm pretty sure
it's something that belonged to your dad.

00:17:09.330 --> 00:17:11.960
An object of ancient origin, made in Mesopotamia...

00:17:12.670 --> 00:17:13.790
Um...

00:17:13.790 --> 00:17:14.880
The whachamacallit rod!

00:17:14.880 --> 00:17:16.540
Mom! How could you totally forget its name?!

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:21.080
From what your dad explained to me,
it's a rod that can multiply the magic power of our clan

00:17:21.080 --> 00:17:24.670
and is very useful since it can transform
into anything with a cylindrical shape!

00:17:24.670 --> 00:17:25.290
Huh?!

00:17:25.500 --> 00:17:29.460
Yikes. That makes it sound like
something tremendously powerful.

00:17:29.630 --> 00:17:31.170
Like a legendary object that must be handled carefully...

00:17:31.420 --> 00:17:33.960
Mrs. Seiko. Can you remember
anything about what it was called?

00:17:34.170 --> 00:17:36.210
Hm... I'm trying to think.

00:17:36.210 --> 00:17:39.420
It was something foreign-sounding
that didn't leave much of an impression.

00:17:40.290 --> 00:17:42.250
Ms. Lilith? Do you remember anything?

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.330
Ancestor!

00:17:44.920 --> 00:17:46.380
Urp, urp, urp...

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.960
Nope. This hangover headache is killing me.

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.380
Don't give up, Ancestor!

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:54.290
Back when my powers were very weak,
I remember Joshua telling me about it in a dream.

00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.960
All I can remember is that it started with an "A"...

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:59.130
The Archfiend's rod? The Accursed rod?

00:17:59.130 --> 00:18:00.790
It wasn't anything like that...

00:18:00.960 --> 00:18:03.000
The Angus-beef rod? The Applesauce rod?

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.130
Nope, something more exotic than that...

00:18:06.920 --> 00:18:07.630
It's weird.

00:18:08.000 --> 00:18:10.830
Why did it suddenly transform when I grabbed it?

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:15.080
I'm guessing that being held by a demon awoken it
from a long period of dormancy.

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:20.500
Apparently, it doesn't even have a base form, which
makes it extremely susceptible to outside influence.

00:18:24.630 --> 00:18:28.000
Joshua mainly used it as a weapon when he had it.

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:32.000
And when it comes to your experience with weaponry,
I'm betting a fork is the first thing to come to mind.

00:18:32.250 --> 00:18:34.790
Listen, Shamiko. You really need to refine
your idea of a weapon.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:37.580
You should start watching more international TV shows!

00:18:37.580 --> 00:18:38.380
TV shows...

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.210
How can you say so much about it,
but still not know its name?

00:18:42.540 --> 00:18:46.330
Since it's something that belonged to Joshua,
I think that your family should keep it.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:47.790
Sounds good.

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:49.880
Thank you so much, Momo.

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:53.040
Don't mention it. My sister is the one
who caused all this, anyway.

00:18:53.040 --> 00:18:54.880
I'm just doing the responsible thing.

00:18:55.130 --> 00:18:56.710
Oh, please don't say that.

00:18:57.000 --> 00:19:00.830
You helped us find a precious family heirloom
that's been missing for years!

00:19:00.830 --> 00:19:03.380
This is progress! We're very appreciative!

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:04.750
Uh, okay then.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.880
We'll finally be able to hang
all 3 of our futons out to dry again.

00:19:11.380 --> 00:19:14.330
Hold up! You were using it as a drying rack before?!

00:19:15.380 --> 00:19:17.630
I'm going to let Yuko hold onto the whachamacallit rod.

00:19:18.500 --> 00:19:22.250
It's an amazing tool with the ability to change
from party prop, to weapon, and even to a drying rack.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:25.540
Please use it to keep yourself
and those you care about safe.

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:28.000
Are you sure that I should have it?

00:19:28.250 --> 00:19:31.460
Well, only a direct descendant
of your dad can actually use it.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:33.880
Just be sure to let me borrow
it as a drying rack sometimes.

00:19:34.420 --> 00:19:37.540
Yahoo! Then I'm gonna try using it right now!

00:19:37.540 --> 00:19:39.080
Come on, whachamacallit rod!

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:40.420
You seem oddly enthusiastic about this.

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:42.290
Well, duh! We're talking about a magic wand here!

